## Adjacency Index — full feature (Tasks 1–7)

Context: Implements a two-table adjacency index (`_adj_out` / `_adj_in`) for
Lakehouse (Delta) and Lakebase (Postgres) backends, wires it into every write
path that mutates the graph (Build, managed-synced apply, reasoning
materialization, cohort edge writes, inference purge), exposes an adjacency-
only refresh action in the UI (Lakehouse Build panel and Lakebase Sync panel),
and documents the feature in the canonical architecture, graphdb-integration,
and user-guide docs. Neo4j is unchanged and has no adjacency tables.

### Changes

1. **src/back/core/graphdb/adjacency.py** — new dialect-aware shared SQL
   module: typed-out / typed-in selects, 1-hop neighbor UNION, and
   `expand_and_fetch_sql` with Spark LEFT ANTI JOIN vs Postgres NOT EXISTS.
   `__all__` declared; raises `ValueError` on empty URI lists; UNION ALL with
   outer DISTINCT.

2. **src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBBackend.py** — adjacency capability hooks:
   `supports_adjacency` (default `False`), `sql_flavor`, `adjacency_table_ids`,
   `rebuild_adjacency`, `adjacency_ready`; `expand_entity_neighbors` branches
   to adjacency SQL when `adjacency_ready`.

3. **src/back/core/graphdb/_starter_kit/ExampleStore.py** — added commented
   optional adjacency override stubs for new engine integrations.

4. **src/back/core/graphdb/delta/_table_naming.py** — added `_adj_out` /
   `_adj_in` FQN and suffix helpers aligned with existing
   `triplestore_<domain>_V<n>` naming.

5. **src/back/core/graphdb/delta/materialize.py** — added
   `build_adj_ctas_sql(spo_fqn, adj_fqn, direction)` with Delta CTAS +
   required clustering (`src` for out, `dst` for in); reuses shared
   `typed_out_select` / `typed_in_select` for semantic parity with fallback.

6. **src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaFlatStore.py** — enabled adjacency
   support (`supports_adjacency`, `sql_flavor`, `adjacency_table_ids`,
   `rebuild_adjacency`); adjacency `OPTIMIZE` is best-effort (warn on error,
   CTAS is hard failure); `expand_and_fetch_subgraph` uses adjacency SQL when
   ready, with SPO fallback; `purge_materialized_triples` triggers full
   adjacency rebuild.

7. **src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaTripleStoreBuildPipeline.py** — wired
   post-build adjacency rebuild after graph VIEW creation and (table mode) after
   `_data` optimize; adjacency failures fail the build; progress messages
   include "Building adjacency index…".

8. **src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/_adjacency_ddl.py** — new module:
   adjacency DDL/rebuild helpers for Lakebase (`CREATE TABLE` + PK + btree
   indexes, `TRUNCATE`/`INSERT`/`ANALYZE`); deterministic identifier bounding
   with hash suffixes (`≤63` bytes); `adjacency_index_name()`;
   `rebuild_adjacency_data` (transactional) + `analyze_adjacency_tables` (post-
   commit).

9. **src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/LakebaseFlatStore.py** — enabled adjacency
   capability; `rebuild_adjacency()` uses explicit `_txn_cursor` transaction for
   atomic data refresh (CTAS hard failure; ANALYZE post-commit); `expand_and_
   fetch_subgraph` with Postgres multi-hop SQL when adjacency ready, SPO-derived
   CTE fallback when missing; `purge_materialized_triples` triggers full
   adjacency rebuild.

10. **src/back/objects/digitaltwin/_build_pipeline.py** — Lakebase-only guard
    (`supports_adjacency` + `sql_flavor == postgres`) triggers adjacency rebuild
    after full rebuild optimize and at end of managed-synced apply; adjacency
    failures are fail-loud, decoupled from companion truncate try-block.

11. **src/back/core/reasoning/ReasoningService.py** — post-insert adjacency
    rebuild guard in `materialize_inferred` after `optimize_inferred_companion`;
    fail-loud semantics.

12. **src/back/core/graph_analysis/CohortBuilder.py** — guarded adjacency
    rebuild in `materialize_to_graph` after successful edge insert (`count > 0`);
    returns inserted count.

13. **src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py** — added thin
    `POST /dtwin/adjacency/refresh` route with per-domain `graph_backend`
    validation, TaskManager task creation, daemon-thread orchestration; no JSON
    body parsing.

14. **src/back/objects/digitaltwin/DigitalTwin.py** — added
    `run_adjacency_refresh_task` worker: opens active store via
    `get_graphdb(domain_snapshot, settings)`, checks adjacency support, resolves
    current graph relation, calls `store.rebuild_adjacency(graph_name)`.

15. **src/front/templates/partials/dtwin/_query_sync.html** — "Refresh
    adjacency" secondary action in Lakebase Sync panel; role-gated (builder /
    admin only, disabled lock variant for other roles).

16. **src/front/templates/partials/dtwin/_query_databricks_build.html** —
    "Refresh adjacency" secondary action in Lakehouse Build panel; same role
    gating.

17. **src/front/static/query/js/query-sync.js** — adjacency task start /
    resume / poll flow (`/dtwin/adjacency/refresh` + `/tasks/{id}`),
    sessionStorage persistence, explicit hide for `neo4j` / `none`, disable
    guards while build/refresh runs or graph has no data; visibility strictly
    `backend === 'lakebase'`.

18. **src/front/static/query/js/query-databricks-build.js** — Lakehouse
    adjacency refresh polling flow, button visibility / state guards,
    `checkAndResumeDatabricksTask` (task-status pre-check before resuming poll),
    status reload on completion.

19. **docs/graphdb-integration.md** — documented adjacency index objects table
    (Lakehouse Delta + Lakebase Postgres), Neo4j unchanged note, and
    adjacency-only refresh semantics per mode.

20. **docs/architecture.md** — added "Adjacency index objects" subsection under
    Lakehouse Unity Catalog objects with per-mode refresh semantics and
    cross-reference.

21. **docs/user-guide.md** — added "Adjacency index snapshot" note in Build
    guidance with per-mode freshness table and caveat on Explorer vs SPARQL
    divergence in table mode.

